<section class="example-section">
  <ul>
    <li>Insert the USB drive into the laptop.</li>
    <li>Find the key to press to select the boot order. Search Google for your laptop's brand and model.</li>
    <li>Select the USB drive to boot from. In the menu that appears, select either <code>Try or Install Ubuntu</code> or <code>Ubuntu safe graphics</code>.</li>
    <li>Follow the instructions. When prompted, choose to erase the disk, enable disk encryption, and set a strong passphrase of at least 5 random words. Add it to your password manager.</li>
    <li>Choose a username and a strong password for the device. Add them to your password manager.</li>
    <li>After completing the instructions, you will be prompted to remove the USB drive and restart. Your laptop will then be ready.</li>
  </ul>
